# ManyFin SQL Complaint Operations Analysis

## Project Overview
SQL analysis of a mock FinTech complaint operations dataset modelled on 
real Tier 2 support workflows in regulated financial environments 
(crypto, FX, equities). Built as part of a career transition portfolio 
targeting CRM Automation and Ops Analyst roles.

## Dataset
- **File:** Fixed_ManyFin.csv
- **Rows:** 41 tickets
- **Period:** June–August 2026
- **Columns:** ticket_id, issue_type, created_date, resolution_date, 
  sla_target, escalation_level, refund_amount, resolution_time

## Business Questions Answered

| Query | Business Question | Key Finding |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | What % of tickets breached SLA? | 50% breach rate (19/38 resolved) |
| 2 | Which issues escalate most? | Crypto Withdrawal hit Tier 2 most (5 tickets) |
| 3 | Which issues cost most in refunds? | FX Exchange Rate Slip: total 906.19 |
| 4 | How did volume trend monthly? | July had worst resolution time (65.29h avg) |
| 5 | Which escalation level is slowest? | Compliance & Risk: 77.46h average |

## SQL Concepts Used
SELECT, FROM, WHERE, GROUP BY, ORDER BY, COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX,
ROUND, CASE WHEN, IS NOT NULL, CAST, strftime, AS

## Files
- `query1_sla_breach_rate.sql`
- `query2_escalation_frequency.sql`
- `query3_refund_by_issue_type.sql`
- `query4_monthly_trend.sql`
- `query5_resolution_by_escalation.sql`
- `Fixed_ManyFin.csv` — source dataset

## Tools Used
